  "body": "If the W3C is allowing href=“” to replace xlink:href=“” in SVG, why isn't the WHATWG allowing href=“” on more elements in HTML?\r\n\r\nI am not suggesting that authors be allowed to use href=“” on all elements, but we could have a discussion and decide which elements it would be allowed on. Not familiar with SVG and MathML but could we allow href=\"\" on more elements in HTML, and then also in SVG and MathML?\r\n\r\nWhat problem am I trying to solve? I think it makes the markup look a lot nicer. Makes the languages more elegant. Reduces the amount of markup required. See Eric Meyer's proposal for more reasons to adopt this:\r\n<a href=\"https://meyerweb.com/eric/html-xhtml/html5-linking.html\">https://meyerweb.com/eric/html-xhtml/html5-linking.html</a>\r\n<a href=\"https://meyerweb.com/eric/thoughts/2008/07/23/any-element-linking-demo/\">https://meyerweb.com/eric/thoughts/2008/07/23/any-element-linking-demo/</a>",
